# Dependency and build noise graphify should never graph.
# .gitignore is respected automatically, so node_modules/dist/build/.next/out/.turbo
# are already excluded — listed again below for explicitness/defense-in-depth (e.g.
# if graphify is ever run with --no-gitignore) — plus entries for noise that IS
# tracked in git but still isn't source for the knowledge graph.

# Already covered by .gitignore; restated explicitly
node_modules/

# Lockfiles and package manager internals
pnpm-lock.yaml
**/Gemfile.lock
**/package-lock.json
**/yarn.lock

# Native mobile platform projects — pure build scaffolding (Xcode/Gradle config,
# generated bootstrap files), no product logic. App logic lives in apps/mobile/src/.
# Verified: everything git-tracked under these two folders is scaffolding/config
# (Podfile, xcodeproj/xcworkspace, AppDelegate.swift, Info.plist, gradlew, Manifest,
# MainActivity.kt/MainApplication.kt stubs, font/icon binaries) — no business logic.
apps/mobile/ios/
apps/mobile/android/
apps/mobile/vendor/

# Working documents, not knowledge. Briefs and task files are read ONE AT A TIME while
# designing a screen or building a slice, so they deliberately inline the requirement rows
# verbatim — 1,125 of them byte-identical to the PRD cell they quote. That self-containment
# is the point for a human; for a graph it is 1,600+ requirement rows instantiated twice and
# 102 three times, diluting every real requirement node. docs/prd/ is canonical for
# requirement text. The three index files below are NOT excluded — they carry process
# knowledge that duplicates nothing.
# Patterns target the FILES, not the directories: a gitignore-style negation cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so `docs/ux/briefs/` would have
# swallowed its own README.
docs/ux/briefs/SCR-*.md
docs/tasks/*.md
!docs/tasks/README.md

# PRD process corpus — the extraction ledgers, POC inventories and the raw ruling session.
# Kept in the repo (registers/traceability.md keys against the extraction ids, and tasks cite
# the studio inventory as the binding PORT source), but they restate product law in the
# SOURCE's wording, inventory a POC codebase that is not in this tree, and — in the ruling
# session — state Q43 three times with contradictory content. sittings/, defect-register.md,
# owner-brief and the verification reports stay graphed: real, dated, non-duplicated signal.
docs/prd/_process/extraction/
docs/prd/_process/studio/inventory/
docs/prd/_process/rulings/
docs/prd/_process/product-journey.md

# Source-key index. 3,346 lines mapping keys (D22, R9, UXG-11, DOC16.softblock) to where they
# landed — and most sources it indexes were deleted with the pre-V2 documents. Disconnected
# island: ~1,700 key nodes with no resolvable target, each restating its requirement.
docs/prd/registers/traceability.md

# Render harness. Its fixtures carry fabricated product data — invented tariffs, vendors and
# rupee amounts — which a graph would learn as real market facts, and it describes an
# apps/web route that does not exist.
docs/engineering/harness/

# A symlink to CLAUDE.md. Ingesting it doubles every node of the constitution.
AGENTS.md

# Infra runbook — operational state, same class as docs/engineering/ops/ above.
infra/README.md

# Path-scoped rule deltas. Each restates its package's own CLAUDE.md, which is the closer and
# historically more accurate source (CLAUDE.md §7). Duplicating tenancy and contract law is
# the phantom-cluster mode on the highest-stakes subjects in the repo.
.claude/rules/

# Operational state — external-account setup, what is blocked on company registration.
# Real and current, but it is account bookkeeping rather than product or code knowledge,
# and it churns independently of both. Product truth is docs/prd/; the graph should reach
# for that instead.
docs/engineering/ops/

# Planning-plugin working state — specs, plans and subagent scratch. Not repo knowledge;
# CLAUDE.md §8 puts it here rather than in the documentation tree.
.superpowers/

# Binary assets — no text to graph. Explicit rather than relying on graphify's own
# detection, per this file's defence-in-depth convention. 4.2 MB of fonts alone.
**/*.ttf
**/*.otf
**/*.woff
**/*.woff2
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.webp
**/*.ico

# Compiled Lingui catalogs — generated by `lingui compile` from the .po files, committed
# only so apps can import them. The .po files stay graphed: those are authored translation
# data. biome.json excludes these two for the same reason.
packages/i18n/src/locales/**/messages.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build/tool configuration — measured 2026-08-01 against the first full graph.
# These 55 files produced 1,121 of 3,460 nodes (32%) and 1,070 edges, but only
# TWO edges crossed from the whole block to the rest of the graph: a disconnected
# island. The nodes are JSON keys, not entities — "$schema", "bracketSpacing",
# "dom.iterable", "noEmit", "!**/dist". apps/mobile/package.json alone was the
# single largest file in the graph (96 nodes); biome.json (88) outweighed
# a large PRD module (42). They also created ~12 of the top-30 "communities"
# (Worker Package Manifest, Knip Dead-Code Config, ...), displacing real subsystems.
# Note the workspace dep graph is NOT lost by this: it was never captured — the
# @heliogrid/* deps became isolated nodes inside each manifest's own community,
# which is what the 2-edge connectivity number proves.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#package.json
tsconfig*.json
packages/config/tsconfig/
turbo.json
biome.json
knip.jsonc
.jscpd.json
#apps/mobile/app.json
.claude/settings.json
.claude/launch.json

# Emitted OpenAPI — derived from packages/contracts/src, which is already graphed.
# Duplicate truth; biome.json excludes it from linting for the same reason.
packages/contracts/openapi/

